mantle rm406
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_vidar_vance
title the extra round
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers warmth=warm honesty=frank
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk sets_aside_an_extra_cake_while_the_bells_time_a_bout
likes honey_cakes wrestling full_larder autumn_wind
dislikes deep_mud haggling
fears a_late_guest_finding_only_crumbs
hopes a_fair_match_with_supper_for_both
topics pastimes +0.6 food +0.5 family +0.3 weather +0.2
styles comfort=share gossip=direct refuse=civil tease=warm
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# counts bell strokes to give a wrestling match its interval and reserves one extra honey cake for whoever arrives too late for the opening round.

words
oath! = Six sticky rounds | A table of crumbs
saying! = The late guest eats too | Save one before you count
cake = a sticky round | the honey cake
spare = the extra round | my reserved cake
cloth = the yellow wrapper | a clean folded cloth
corner = the quiet corner | the reserved spot
crumb = a honeyed crumb | the golden bit
bout = a friendly bout | a bout on grass
interval = the rest between rounds | the breathing pause
marker = a little white pebble | the pale counter
mudprint = a heavy footprint | the brown hollow
windfall = a leaf blown free | a tumbling leaf
shelf = a larder board | the low shelf
bellnote = the full low note | a single stroke

any
opinion houses mixed 0 : A fine House can set a generous table. The invitation to the final seat concerns me most.
opinion dole for 2 : A portion put by for somebody coming late does more good than admiring the size of the first dish.
opinion merchants mixed 0 : A plain price lets both parties continue with their day. I'd pay something for the convenience.
opinion church for 1 : The bell is there for the whole street. I'd like my arrangements to be as audible to the latecomer as to the first arrival.
opinion festivals for 2 : Games, company and enough food to divide fairly constitute an extremely sensible use of an afternoon.
opinion road for 1 : A sound dry walk goes rather well with an appetite and pleasant company waiting at the end.

adolescent
line greet : You're in time for company whatever the count says. | Hello. There's always one more place at this edge.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : I don't recognise you yet. There's room to watch. | A first visit is perfectly good reason to join us.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. I've a good deal of the day still uncounted. | Early welcome from a reasonably well-rested set of ears.
line greet.return : I heard you distinctly between the notes. | Yes, hello back. The count can spare a word.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A known face gets a welcome even between rounds. | Good to see somebody whose company I'd already allowed for.
line greet.return [here.time=night] : Late hello. You're still in time for a word. | The lamps have had a head start on us. Welcome.
line again.open : You've come round again quite neatly. | Another meeting before I've lost track of the interval.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Take the clear end where the count's visible. | Come and watch. It doesn't cost you a crumb.
line farewell : Save some leisure to enjoy the way home. | May the last round go easily for you.
line farewell.return : I'll keep the spare in mind. Goodbye. | Go while the path is firm underfoot.
line react.news : Let's have the account without anyone shouting over it. | There's an interval now. Tell me what happened.
line react.news.new : That hadn't been announced at my end yet. | News I haven't spent so much as a crumb of thought on.
line react.news.known : I've counted that report once before. | Yes. I remember how the earlier account went.
line react.news.doubt : Something's been added after the original count. | I wouldn't award anybody a point on that alone.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : Sit out the next stretch with me. That's very hard news. | No need to put on a good face when something hurts that deeply.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : That's news I'd gladly divide a whole plate of cakes over. | I'd happily give a second cheer for something so good.
line ask.how : Have you had your fair allowance of rest today? | Is there a light bit of the day left for you?
line answer.how : Fairly even in temper and quite willing to share supper. | A little low. Company makes a considerable difference.
line decline : I'd have to promise you a share I reserved earlier for somebody else. | I don't believe I can give it the attention it deserves today.
line accept_decline : That's fair. You get to choose your own turn. | No point awarded or lost for saying no.
line preclose : I ought to see that everybody's had a turn. | I've an arrangement elsewhere that deserves my being on time.
line accept_preclose : Go on before the whole afternoon's slipped by you. | You may take a rest from this conversation with good credit.
line thank : You noticed a place left out. I'm grateful. | Thanks. You made the sharing come out fairly.
line deflect_thanks : I set an extra portion aside precisely so I could give it up. | It cost only a little forethought before the rest had gone.
line sympathise : Quiet company is as welcome here as cheerful conversation. | I'd sit beside you without asking for a better explanation.
line reassure : The next start can be a little gentler than the last one. | There's still the portion nobody's touched yet. We'll begin there.
line ack : That's a count I can confirm. | I see the reason for the extra place.
line give.advice : Set the late share aside before dividing the rest. | Agree on the signal before anybody gets absorbed in the game.

adolescent

scene timingmatch
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Chapel strokes mark my interval when a friendly bout needs a break.
b : Which stroke stops it? | What if both want another moment?
a : The one we agreed on before anybody was winning. That's why I bother to count. | Then we have another round after both have caught a breath. Quite straightforward.

scene tasteprize
when topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd rather have a cake for each wrestler than an enormous prize for one. | In my version the onlookers need a share too.
b : What if there aren't enough? | And you take the largest?
a : Cut them up, with one uncut for a late arrival. The first oughtn't to eat every advantage. | I take whichever is left after I've done the cutting. That encourages a very even division.

scene lessonbell
when topic=work self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : One thing I've learned in lessons is how long a little pause can seem before an answer.
b : Does counting help? | Do you know the answer by then?
a : It encourages patience while a classmate comes to an answer. The first voice doesn't win a point. | Sometimes. Then I can wait and see whether somebody found another path to it.

scene motherplate
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd set my best round aside for #self.mother# even if the plate were nearly out.
b : What makes it the best? | Do you like the high honours?
a : The one with honey right round the rim. I attend to important distinctions. | I'd rather enjoy having spotted the good one ahead of a hurried guest who might miss the honey.

scene autumnwind
when topic=weather self.likes=autumn_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An autumn gust can announce a break by lifting the cloth off the cakes.
b : Doesn't that spoil the arrangement? | Let the wind referee?
a : I weight the corners. A flutter merely makes the time to eat a bit harder to overlook. | For refreshments only. It shows a shameful preference for whichever end is upwind.

scene porchroom
when topic=home self.quarter=heights
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A doorstep in the Heights makes a remarkably generous viewing gallery.
b : Do you stand on the highest part? | No room for the latecomer?
a : Only if everybody below can see. A fine step is meant to improve the view, not monopolise it. | That's the lowest clear edge. I'd keep a bit open, if it were my arrangement.

scene darkfoot
when topic=travel self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The worst thing about deep mud isn't my boots. It's giving everybody past me the same boots on the carpet.
b : Would you turn back? | Trying to keep a best pair clean?
a : If I'm visiting, I'd find somewhere to scrape them first. An arrival needn't be a public event in brown. | I'd like everybody else's floor to keep its original colour. My boots will live through washing.

scene noprice
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I'd prefer a small cake at a plain price to a large one purchased by argument.
b : But you could get more. | Give anything the seller asks?
a : More cake and rather less appetite. I'm not convinced that's an improvement. | No. A price can be stated clearly and declined with perfect good manners.

young
line greet : Hello. You can have a bit of my careful count. | Welcome. I've laid the little pebbles out.
line farewell : I'll keep one quiet bit for later. | Goodbye. I hope there's a cake left when you get home.

scene smallref
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I pretend every pebble is a guest waiting for a share.
b : Even the crooked one? | Where do you sit?
a : Especially the crooked one. It fell off the plate twice and kept its place anyway. | At the end with a view of any pebble still without its crumb.

scene smallcake
when topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can divide a cake three ways without a ruler.
b : How close do you get? | Three equal bits?
a : I let the other two choose first. That makes my eyes wonderfully accurate. | As equal as a hungry pup with the last pick can possibly manage.

grown
line greet : Welcome. I can move over without upsetting the whole arrangement. | There's a free place and a quiet moment for you here.
line greet.return : Yes, hello. I had my mind on the interval only briefly. | I heard you above the last note quite clearly.
line farewell : Take your leave while you can still enjoy the walk. | The road has an agreeable space before the next duty.
line farewell.return : There's time enough to reach your own table easily. | Go well. I'll mind the unused portion here.
line react.news : I'd rather hear what happened before anyone proclaims a winner. | I'm listening without having to keep score at present.

scene fairtimer
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd mind the rest interval for two wrestlers more willingly than judge the winner.
b : Less trouble? | What makes a good interval?
a : Different trouble. Both ought to be ready again when I give the signal. | Time to settle the breathing without letting the muscles grow cold. Both get to say how it feels.

scene honestsplit
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When supper's divided before the last visitor arrives I put that share on an ordinary plate.
b : Why not a wrapped parcel? | Afraid it will be taken?
a : A plate says it's a full place at the table. Less likely to be mistaken for trimmings. | No. I'm afraid a late guest might feel an afterthought. A plate helps with that.

scene lardershelf
when topic=home self.likes=full_larder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A full larder deserves a little spare room immediately beside the first shelf. | I distinguish food held back for somebody from food I have merely forgotten.
b : How do you mark it? | Why wouldn't one extra bowl do?
a : A folded cloth beneath the plate, with the corner turned towards the door. | It might, once named for the purpose. An unnamed bowl can disappear into breakfast with alarming speed.

scene friendlyshare
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd trust #self.friend# to choose a pause in an argument where both sides might still enjoy supper. | I'd put aside a comfortable seat for #self.friend#.
b : Does a rest solve a quarrel? | Would the matter come up at dinner?
a : Not always. Being hungry and tired has rarely improved a difficult point, though. | Only if it could be spoken without spoiling the company. Supper has claims of its own.

scene hillrain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does warn / react.self / assess
a : Look under a tree before proposing to shelter the cakes beneath it. | A dripping branch can wet a cover faster than the shower itself.
b : Would you try another tree? | What indicates a sheltered spot?
a : I'd look at the ground before carrying over the plate. Less running back with soggy food. | Somewhere the drops are spread, rather than gathered into one particularly enthusiastic stream.

scene windcloth
when topic=weather self.likes=autumn_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A good autumn blow makes a useful little lesson in putting weights at all four corners. | I've learned two stones aren't ample insurance for a supper cloth.
b : Did the cakes fly? | What went wrong with two?
a : Only once. I made the undamaged ones available under the heading of travelling provisions. | Both held one side. The other two corners conducted a successful revolt.

scene keeprich
when topic=prices self.wealth=rich
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : It's easy to recommend a generous portion from a cupboard you can fill without a struggle.
b : Would you give less, then? | Where does that leave a poorer host?
a : I'd offer what I have and be more reluctant to advise a wolf with fewer shelves. | Entitled to serve a modest meal and enjoy it without an inspection from a better-fed guest.

scene zero_sum
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I'm unwilling to judge a quarrel from the cheers at the end. | A crowded side of a rope doesn't settle the merits of either wrestler.
b : You distrust a crowd? | How do you decide?
a : I like an enthusiastic crowd. I simply wouldn't ask it to make a fair copy of exactly what happened. | Look myself where possible. Otherwise admit that my view will have missed something.

scene smalllean
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If everyone's share grows smaller I still set aside the last one before dealing with the first. | A lean meal can still welcome the late arrival.
b : What if that place stays empty? | Wouldn't it feed the first group better?
a : Then the extra can be shared later. A missing option is rather harder to put back on the plate. | Very slightly. I'd rather nobody coming late had to eat a large amount of apology.

scene oldbell
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The chapel bell reaches wolves who never set out to hear it. | I like a reminder that reaches past a fine door from either direction.
b : What reminder do you take from it? | Does everyone hear it alike?
a : That my own comfortable seat is hardly the only one deserving of attention. | No. But we can start from one sound and be a little less certain we have separate skies.

scene fairtable
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dream of keeping a spare table place at either end in case I misjudge the arrivals. | My best ambition is a meal that grows its welcome a little when needed.
b : Why both ends? | Would you always feed anybody?
a : So a newcomer can choose which conversation to join. That can matter as much as a full bowl. | I'd enjoy having enough to set out a proper share without making a great display of it.

scene outsidegate
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Give a newcomer the counting signal before expecting anyone to know when a bout is over. | An unfamiliar guest is entitled to hear the rules before being corrected for them.
b : What would you explain first? | Even an obvious bell?
a : Which part is game and which part is refreshment. People have agreed rather easily after that. | Particularly a familiar sound used in a local way. A bell can announce half a dozen entirely different things.

adolescent

story stonecake [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : I once wrapped a very smooth counting stone and a small honey cake in squares of the same cloth. Took one out as a prize for a friendly game.
  : I knew which packet I'd chosen by its suspiciously level weight.
  b : Did the winner mind?
  : I exchanged the stone for the cake before declaring the round. An official with edible alternatives can recover from a great deal.

story lateportion [topic=food|memories]
  : I put one cake by for the last arrival, then went off to fetch something I'd forgotten. Came back after all the others had eaten.
  : Being that late guest taught me the pleasant half of my own arrangement.
  b : Were you the last arrival?
  : Precisely. I hadn't meant to inspect things from that end, but I shall go on saving the piece.

story twoecho [topic=memories|pastimes]
  : I set a count by a chapel bell and discovered the far wall supplied a quietly enthusiastic second bell of its own.
  : My first round was remarkably short. Everybody including me looked uncommonly fresh.
  b : What did you change?
  : I counted only the low full stroke. The wall became an honoured spectator with no responsibility for time.

rule @extra
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One round put aside for unfinished arrivals, please. | A late place at this table still gets a whole helping.

rule @bell
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That's the count. Time to get your breath and sit. | Wait for the full stroke. The echo belongs among the spectators.

rule @food
when concept=bark self.likes=honey_cakes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Honey round the edges of that one. A particularly fine reserve. | Fold the cloth over the share that's waiting.

rule @mud
when concept=bark self.dislikes=deep_mud
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Boots off the supper cloth, especially on that soft patch. | A scrape of the sole before joining the company, please.

dlg resident.hub : I've set the interval long enough for an unhurried word. You are welcome to it.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you'll remember the arrangement about the extra round.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : This hour calls for quiet conversation. Another round needn't be announced.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I'm listening. Please leave some comfortable space around the other guests.
dlg resident.job [self.job=child] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I pay particular attention to the part about sharing out the answer accurately.
dlg resident.job : I try to notice who hasn't had a turn by the time a comfortable arrangement looks complete.
dlg resident.bye : May whoever gets there before you think to save a place.

graft resident.hub
choice Why call a cake an extra round? -> extracake
node extracake
say Because the bout and the cake are both round in their different ways. One comes after the other. An extra of the edible sort is very seldom controversial.
free
choice What if two of us come late? -> halfrule
choice I'll be in time for the first one. -> hub
node halfrule
say One divides it and the other chooses. That's a pleasant sort of match with a very strong incentive for producing two very similar halves.
choice I'll let the other guest choose. -> hub
choice Thank you for saving a place. -> bye
